title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1952 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Sordland.

= Inter-Party Relationships

Sometimes to form Government a coalition is necessary with other parties,or perhaps we can stand alone.


- @USP: Strengthen our bonds with the USP.
- @WPB: Strengthen our bonds with the Bludish Worker's Party.
- @CPS: Work towards repairing relationships with the Communist Party.
- @SLP: Improve relations with the laissez-faire party.
- @spd_alone: The PFJP can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@USP
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; usp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); usp_reform += 0.01


@CPS
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; cps_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The Communists had originally split from us,it may be beneficial to repair relations with them.

@WPB
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources
on-arrival: wpb_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The WPB share some of our goals,it could be helpful if they have friendly relations with us.Especially in establishing social equality 

@SLP
subtitle: -1 resources, don't 
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources
on-arrival: slp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

This is a waste of resources. Why are you like this?

@spd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
